subnapi (0.5.4-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Report a failed search honestly: a server that could not be reached, and
    Napisy24 refusing the account details, are no longer both presented as
    "no subtitles found".
  * Apply a network timeout. A server that accepted a connection and then
    said nothing held every request open indefinitely, and closing a dialog
    joins those threads - one silent server locked up the application.
  * Repeat NapiProjekt's stated reason when it refuses an upload, instead of
    only that it was refused.
  * Stop sending the NapiProjekt password with the directory scan's database
    check, which ignores credentials entirely, and use HTTPS for NapiProjekt
    and Napisy24 throughout.
  * Fix encoding handling: replacing diacritics no longer writes UTF-8 into a
    file of another encoding, removing advertising lines keeps the file's own
    line endings, and an encoding named in the configuration but no longer
    supported falls back to the default instead of silently disabling
    conversion.
  * Check that 7-Zip actually succeeded rather than only that it finished.
  * Subtitles fetched through a napiprojekt: link now go through the same
    post-processing as any other.
  * Reject a command-line switch whose value is missing or is another switch,
    rather than uploading that switch as the subtitle author.
  * Tell a failed database check apart from a confirmed miss in the
    NapiProjekt directory scan.

 -- mskpluk <mskpluk@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 15 Aug 2026 20:00:00 +0000

subnapi (0.5.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * OpenSubtitles: fetch subtitle files over HTTP instead of the XML-RPC
    download method, which stopped returning subtitles - for accounts
    without VIP it answers with a placeholder advertising VIP membership,
    which was saved next to the movie as if it were the subtitles.
  * OpenSubtitles: match results by release name and fall back to searching
    by file name when no subtitles carry the movie's hash, honouring the
    other releases uploaders list in their comment.
  * Fix encoding auto-detection always answering UTF-8, which decoded
    windows-1250 subtitles into replacement characters.
  * NapiProjekt directory scan: tell a failed database check apart from a
    confirmed miss, instead of offering files for upload that may already
    be in the database.

 -- mskpluk <mskpluk@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 15 Aug 2026 14:00:00 +0000

